---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Projects, invite, and Access Inspector — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">For Team admins</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Projects, invite, and Access Inspector</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <p>
                Presence on the team is membership. The only team role to pick is Team
                admin (a flag). You create and archive projects in <strong class="text-foreground">that team only</strong>.
                You are treated as Project admin on every project in the team. If a
                department does not want that inherit, they split into two teams.
            </p>

            <h2>Administration shell</h2>
            <p>
                Footer switches Workspace ↔ Administration. Administration dashboard is
                the current team: counts, pending invites, recent failed runs, create-project
                CTA. Switching team reloads a clean home. Developers hitting /Admin are
                redirected to Workspace with a toast.
            </p>
            <p>
                Creating a team does not auto-seed a project (Platform admin does team
                create). An empty team is valid. Switching to it clears ProjectId. Workspace
                for you then offers Create project; a member with no placement sees “ask a
                team admin”.
            </p>

            <h2>Invite and add</h2>
            <p>
                Invite creates the Identity user immediately (unusable password,
                EmailConfirmed false), assigns team and optional project memberships in
                the same transaction, then emails a hashed single-use token. Accept only
                sets the password. SMTP must be configured; invite send fails closed if
                mail cannot be sent. Pending invitees cannot sign in. Roles may still be
                edited while pending.
            </p>
            <p>
                Existing confirmed users are added: memberships apply now, notification
                email, no accept. You cannot grant Platform admin or invite another team
                (including a second team in the same request). Grant ceiling is enforced
                even if the picker UI were wrong.
            </p>
            <p>
                Remove from team cascades: project memberships in that team's projects
                go away. Other teams and the login stay. If the user is still pending and
                has no remaining teams and is not Platform admin, the pending user is
                revoked. Confirmed users with zero teams get the empty-state page, not
                account deletion.
            </p>
            <p>
                Cannot remove or demote the last enabled Team admin of a team.
            </p>

            <h2>Access Inspector</h2>
            <p>
                Read-only effective-access explainability for Platform admin and Team
                admin (team-scoped). Pickers use searchable overlays. It does not edit
                grants.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
